      "schema:description": "Describes the typical amount of work for hourly employees. This data does not apply to salary employees. 40 - Employee paid on an hourly basis; works an 8 hour day; can be either full-time permanent (FT/P) or full-time temporary (FT-T) which is a seasonal employee; 35 - Employee paid on an hourly basis; works a 7 hour day; can be either full-time permanent (FT/P) or full-time temporary (FT-T) which is a seasonal employee; 20 - Employee paid on a part-time, hourly basis; typically works a 4 hour day, 5 days a week; 10 - Employee paid on a part-time, hourly basis; works 10 hours or less in a week.",
